{{also|Tribute|tributé}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm}}, from {{der|en|fro|tribut}}, from {{der|en|la|tributum|t=tribute|lit=a thing contributed or paid}}, neuter of {{m|la|tributus}}, past participle of {{m|la|tribuere|t=to assign, allot, grant, give, bestow, etc.}}, usually derived, from {{m|la|tribus||tribe}}. See {{m|en|tribe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɹɪbjuːt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-tribute.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An [[acknowledgment]] of [[gratitude]], [[respect]] or [[admiration]]; an [[accompanying]] [[gift]].
#: ''Please accept this as a '''tribute''' of our thanks.''
#* Gray
#*: the passing '''tribute''' of a sigh
## An [[homage]] made in a [[body of work]] to another work or [[creator]].
##: ''Did you catch the ''Up in Smoke'' '''tribute''' in that episode of ''That '70s Show''?''
# A [[payment]] made by one [[nation]] to another in [[submission]].
#: ''The Ancient Romans made their conquered countries pay '''tribute'''.''
# [[extortion|Extortion]]; [[protection]] [[money]].
# A payment made by a [[feudal]] [[vassal]] to his [[lord]].
# {{lb|en|mining}} A certain proportion of the mined [[ore]], or of its [[value]], given to the [[miner]] as [[payment]].
#: {{rfquotek|en|Pryce}}
#: {{rfquotek|en|Tomlinson}}

